CAT = "sfadminObjects"; SEG = "OBJ"
Q = [
('Inspection records must be deleted when their property record is deleted, and must always have a property. Which relationship fits?',
 'Master-detail', ['Lookup', 'Hierarchical', 'External lookup'],
 'In a master-detail relationship the detail always needs a master, and deleting the master deletes its details. A lookup is optional and does not cascade.'),
('Where can a roll-up summary field be created?',
 'On the master object', ['On the detail object', 'On any lookup parent', 'On the User object'],
 'Roll-up summary fields sit on the master of a master-detail relationship and summarise its detail records (some standard relationships also allow them).'),
('Which calculations can a roll-up summary field perform?',
 'COUNT, SUM, MIN and MAX', ['AVERAGE and MEDIAN only', 'Any formula function at all', 'Text joins of child names'],
 'Roll-up summaries count detail records or take the sum, minimum or maximum of a field on them, optionally with filter criteria.'),
('Students and courses have a many-to-many relationship. How is this modelled?',
 'A junction object', ['A lookup on each side', 'A roll-up summary', 'A record type'],
 'A junction object with two master-detail relationships, one to each object, links many records on one side to many on the other.'),
('On a junction object, which master-detail relationship sets the look and owner of its records?',
 'The first one created', ['The second one created', 'The one with more records', 'The one chosen by the user'],
 "The first master-detail relationship created on a junction object is the primary one; it controls the junction record's look and feel and ownership."),
('An admin tries to change a lookup field to master-detail, but Salesforce blocks it. What is the most likely reason?',
 'Some records have it blank', ['The object already has a tab', 'The field has help text set', 'A report already uses the object'],
 'A lookup can become master-detail only when every existing record has a value in the lookup field, because detail records always need a master.'),
('Which relationship type is available only on the User object?',
 'Hierarchical', ['Master-detail', 'Lookup', 'Many-to-many'],
 'A hierarchical relationship is a special lookup from a user to another user, such as a custom manager field.'),
("A validation rule's error formula evaluates to true when a user saves a record. What happens?",
 'The save is blocked', ['The record saves with a warning', 'The field is cleared', 'An email goes to the admin'],
 'A validation rule blocks the save and shows its error message whenever its formula returns true.'),
('A discount over 20% must not be saved unless a reason is entered. What is the simplest declarative way?',
 'A validation rule', ['A roll-up summary field', 'A sharing rule', 'A compact layout'],
 'A validation rule such as Discount above 0.2 with the reason blank stops the save and tells the user what to fix.'),
('Which field type shows a value calculated from other fields and cannot be edited by users?',
 'Formula field', ['Auto-number field', 'External ID field', 'Picklist field'],
 'Formula fields are read only and calculate their value each time the record is viewed, from fields on the record or on its parent records.'),
("A formula on Contact shows the account's industry. What kind of formula is this?",
 'A cross-object formula', ['A roll-up summary field', 'A lookup filter on Contact', 'A validation rule on Account'],
 'Cross-object formulas reference fields on related parent records, here Account.Industry from the contact.'),
('Different sales teams need different Stage values and different page layouts on opportunities. What should the admin use?',
 'Record types', ['Field sets', 'Compact layouts', 'Global value sets'],
 'Record types let each team have its own picklist values, business process and page layout, assigned to profiles.'),
('For opportunities, what controls which Stage values a record type offers?',
 'A sales process', ['A support process', 'A lead process', 'A path setting'],
 'Opportunity record types each use a sales process, which lists the stages available. Cases use support processes and leads use lead processes.'),
('What decides which page layout a user sees on a record?',
 'Profile and record type', ['Role and record owner', 'App and tab settings', 'Sharing rules and role'],
 'Page layout assignments map each profile and record type combination to a layout.'),
('A field should appear on the account page only when Type is Customer. Which feature does this without a second layout?',
 'Dynamic Forms', ['Compact layouts', 'Field-level security', 'A record type'],
 'Dynamic Forms place fields and sections on the Lightning record page itself, with visibility rules such as Type equals Customer.'),
('A Close Case button should appear only while a case is open. Which feature fits?',
 'Dynamic Actions', ['A page layout', 'A global action', 'A list view'],
 'Dynamic Actions let the admin show or hide actions on a Lightning record page using filters on record fields, the device or the user.'),
("Which layout controls the fields in a record's highlights panel and in mobile record previews?",
 'Compact layout', ['Page layout', 'Search layout', 'Mini page layout'],
 'Compact layouts set the key fields shown in the highlights panel at the top of a Lightning record page and on mobile cards.'),
('A new Lightning record page should apply only to sales users in the Sales app. How should the admin activate it?',
 'App, record type and profile', ['As the org default for all users', 'As the app default only', 'By role in the hierarchy'],
 'Lightning record pages can be assigned as the org default, the app default, or for a specific app, record type and profile combination.'),
('Which page types can be built in Lightning App Builder?',
 'App, Home and Record pages', ['Only Home pages', 'Only Record pages for objects', 'Email templates and report pages'],
 'Lightning App Builder builds app pages, Home pages and record pages, plus some other page types depending on features enabled.'),
('A Log a Call action should be available from anywhere in the app, not tied to one object. What type of action is this?',
 'A global action', ['An object-specific action', 'A list view button', 'A flow trigger'],
 'Global actions can be used anywhere actions are supported and create records that are not automatically related to a parent record.'),
('A custom field was deleted by mistake two days ago. What can the admin do?',
 'Undelete it from Deleted Fields', ['Nothing, the field and data are gone', 'Restore it from the Recycle Bin', 'Ask users to enter it again'],
 "Deleted custom fields stay in the object's Deleted Fields list for 15 days, during which the admin can undelete them with their data."),
('Three objects need the same list of region values, kept in one place. What should the admin create?',
 'A global value set', ['A dependent picklist', 'A record type', 'A formula field'],
 'A global value set is a shared list of picklist values that several picklist fields can use, so changes are made once.'),
('The City picklist should show only cities in the State the user picked. What is State in this setup?',
 'The controlling field', ['The dependent field', 'A lookup filter on City', 'A field set on the layout'],
 'In a dependent picklist the controlling field (State) filters the values available in the dependent field (City).'),
('A lookup to Account should only let users pick accounts of type Partner. What should the admin add?',
 'A lookup filter', ['A validation rule on Account', 'A sharing rule', 'A record type'],
 'Lookup filters restrict which records can be chosen in a lookup field, and can be required or optional.'),
('A field must be filled in every time a record is saved, including through the API and imports. Where should it be made required?',
 'On the field itself', ['On the page layout', 'In the compact layout', 'In a list view'],
 'Making a field required in its definition enforces it everywhere. Page layout required only applies when users edit through that layout.'),
('Which tool shows objects, fields and relationships as a diagram and lets the admin add fields there?',
 'Schema Builder', ['Lightning App Builder', 'Object Manager list view', 'Report Builder'],
 'Schema Builder displays the data model visually and can create objects, fields and relationships by drag and drop.'),
('Which feature guides users through opportunity stages with key fields and tips at each step?',
 'Path', ['Compact layout', 'Global action', 'Kanban'],
 'Path shows the stages of a picklist as a chevron bar, with key fields and guidance for success at each stage.'),
('A component on a record page should appear only for users with a certain permission. What does the admin set?',
 'A component visibility filter', ['A sharing rule on the object', 'A page layout section', 'A record type for those users'],
 'Component visibility filters in Lightning App Builder show or hide a component by record field, device, permission or user attribute.'),
('Each invoice needs a unique number that Salesforce assigns in sequence. Which field type fits?',
 'Auto Number', ['Formula', 'Number with a default', 'External ID text'],
 'Auto Number fields assign a sequential, read-only value to each new record using a display format such as INV-{0000}.'),
('Users of a new custom object say they cannot open it from the navigation bar. What has the admin most likely forgotten?',
 'A custom tab for the object', ['A master-detail field to Account', 'A roll-up summary field', 'A compact layout for mobile'],
 "A custom object needs a tab before users can add it to an app's navigation, along with object permissions."),
]
